The symbolizer's internals. `mapped_image` is one ELF file it mapped: its sections
(`trace::impl::debug_image`, layer 3) and where its code runs, as a bias and an address range.
The executable is one, every shared object ca's loader held when the symbolizer was made is
another.

`loaded_objects` is how the symbolizer learns of those objects without depending on the
loader: an atomic pointer to a function visiting each of them (`loaded_object`: path, device
and inode, bias, range), null until `ca::dl` loads something. The symbolizer maps each file
again by its path and keeps it only when its device and inode still match, so a file replaced
since it was loaded is left out rather than read wrong.
